\section{Meeting Instructions for Unit Owners}

\begin{center}
{\large\bfseries\color{navyblue} {{ association_name | tex_escape }} }\\[4pt]
{\large {{ meeting_year }} Annual Meeting --- Instructions for Attendees}
\end{center}

\vspace{0.15in}

\subsection*{Before the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Review this packet.} Read the notice, agenda, and any proposed resolutions carefully before the meeting.

{% if election.election_required %}
\item \textbf{Review candidates.} Candidate biographical sketches are included in this packet.
  You may vote in person at the meeting or submit a proxy to designate how your vote should be cast.
{% endif %}

\item \textbf{Submit your proxy (if not attending).} If you cannot attend in person, please complete and return
  the proxy form included in this packet to ensure your unit's vote is represented.
{% if meeting.proxy_deadline %}
  \textbf{Proxy deadline: {{ meeting.proxy_deadline | format_date }}.}
{% endif %}

\item \textbf{Review the financial documents.} The financial summary is included. Detailed financial records
  are available for inspection by appointment with management.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{At the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Sign in.} Please sign the attendance/registration sheet upon arrival.
{% if meeting.registration_time %}
  Registration opens at \textbf{ {{ meeting.registration_time }} }.
{% endif %}

\item \textbf{Quorum.} The meeting will begin once quorum is confirmed. Quorum requires the presence,
  in person or by proxy, of owners representing
  {% if meeting.quorum_threshold %}\textbf{ {{ meeting.quorum_threshold }}\% } of the total votes.{% else %}the minimum number of votes required by the governing documents.{% endif %}
  If quorum is not present when the meeting is called, the chair will announce adjournment procedures.

\item \textbf{One vote per unit.} Each unit is entitled to one vote. If a unit has multiple owners,
  they collectively cast one vote.

\item \textbf{Decorum.} The meeting is conducted under the authority of the presiding officer.
  Please be courteous and allow each speaker to finish. Questions and comments are heard during
  the designated portions of the agenda.

\item \textbf{New Business.} Items of new business may be raised during the New Business portion
  of the agenda. Action on new business items is subject to quorum and procedural requirements.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Proxy Holders}

If you are serving as a proxy holder for another unit owner:
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
\item Bring the signed proxy form.
\item Present it to the registration desk upon arrival.
\item Vote according to any specific directions given on the proxy, or as you see fit if no direction is given.
\end{itemize}

{% if meeting.virtual_option %}
\subsection*{Virtual / Remote Participation}

{% if meeting.virtual_link %}
This meeting will be accessible remotely at: \textbf{ {{ meeting.virtual_link | tex_escape }} }
{% else %}
Remote participation instructions will be distributed separately. Please contact management for access details.
{% endif %}
Remote participants may be subject to limitations on voting depending on the governing documents
and meeting procedures. Confirm voting procedures with management in advance.

{% endif %}

\subsection*{After the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Minutes.} Meeting minutes will be prepared and distributed to all unit owners within
  the time required by the governing documents.

{% if jx.include_org_meeting_note %}
\item \textbf{Organizational Meeting.} The Board will hold its Organizational Meeting immediately following
  the Annual Meeting to elect officers. Unit owners are welcome to observe.
{% endif %}

\item \textbf{Contact information.}
  For questions about this packet or the Annual Meeting, contact
  {% if management_contact %}\textbf{ {{ management_contact | tex_escape }} }{% else %}the Association's management{% endif %}
  {% if management_email %}at {{ management_email | tex_escape }}{% endif %}
  {% if management_phone %}or {{ management_phone | tex_escape }}{% endif %}.
\end{itemize}
